Fonts embedded in the HTML report (ziffer-scan --report)

The report is ONE file that loads nothing, so these three files are read at
render time and written into its stylesheet as base64 @font-face sources
(src/report/fonts.ts). They are not fetched from anywhere.

schibsted-grotesk-400-900.woff2
  Schibsted Grotesk, variable, weights 400 to 900, Latin subset.
  Version 1.100 (built with gftools, the Google Fonts build).
  Copyright 2023 The Schibsted-Grotesk Project Authors
  (https://github.com/schibsted/schibsted-grotesk).
  Licence: SIL Open Font License 1.1.

ibm-plex-mono-400.woff2
ibm-plex-mono-500.woff2
  IBM Plex Mono Regular and Medium, Latin subset. Version 2.3.
  Copyright 2017 IBM Corp., with Reserved Font Name "Plex"
  (https://github.com/IBM/plex).
  Licence: SIL Open Font License 1.1.

Where they came from: copied unchanged from the report's approved design
prototype (report-v2, 2026-09-28). The version and copyright above are read
from each file's own name table, not from memory. The files are distributed
unmodified, under their own names inside the font, which the licence allows.

OFL.txt beside this file is the licence text, with both copyright lines.
Both are listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.attribution.md of this package and of
@ziffer-io/mcp, which renders the same report.
